#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:767
msgid "Fog"
msgstr "Brouillard"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:771
msgid ""
"This section refers to non-volumetric fog only. It is possible to use both "
"non-volumetric fog and :ref:`doc_volumetric_fog` at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:775
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Fog, as in real life, makes distant objects fade away into a uniform color. "
"There are two kinds of fog in Godot:"
msgstr ""
"Le brouillard, comme dans la vie réelle, fait disparaître des objets "
"éloignés dans une couleur uniforme. L'effet physique est en fait assez "
"complexe, mais Godot fournit une bonne approximation. Il y a deux sortes de "
"brouillard dans Godot :"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:778
msgid ""
"**Depth Fog:** This one is applied based on the distance from the camera."
msgstr ""
"**Depth Fog:** Celui-ci est appliqué en fonction de la distance de la caméra."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:779
msgid ""
"**Height Fog:** This one is applied to any objects below (or above) a "
"certain height, regardless of the distance from the camera."
msgstr ""
"**Height Fog:** Celui-ci est appliqué à tout objet situé au-dessous (ou au-"
"dessus) d'une certaine hauteur, quelle que soit la distance qui le sépare de "
"la caméra."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:784
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Both of these fog types can have their curves tweaked, making their "
"transition more or less sharp."
msgstr ""
"Ces deux types de brouillard peuvent avoir leur courbe modifiée, ce qui rend "
"leur transition plus ou moins nette."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:786
msgid "Two properties can be tweaked to make the fog effect more interesting:"
msgstr ""
"Deux propriétés peuvent être modifiées pour rendre l’effet de brouillard "
"plus intéressant :"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:788
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first is **Sun Scatter**, which makes use of the DirectionalLight3D's "
"color and energy in the current scene. When looking toward the directional "
"light (usually a sun), the fog will be tinted according to the light's color "
"to simulate the sunlight passing through the fog."
msgstr ""
"La première est **Sun amount**, qui utilise la propriété Sun Color du "
"brouillard. En regardant vers une lumière directionnelle (généralement un "
"soleil), la couleur du brouillard sera changée, simulant la lumière du "
"soleil passant à travers le brouillard."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:793
msgid ""
"The second is **Aerial Perspective**, which tints the fog color according to "
"the sky color to better blend the sky with the background. Higher values "
"will result in more tinting, with ``1.0`` fully replacing the regular fog "
"color with aerial perspective. This can be used in large open world levels "
"to provide a better sense of depth, or to avoid color discontinuities "
"between the sky and fog colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:799
msgid ""
"If both **Sun Scatter** and **Aerial Perspective** are greater than ``0.0``, "
"sun scattering is applied on top of aerial perspective."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:804
msgid ""
"Fog can cause banding to appear on the viewport, especially at higher "
"density levels. See :ref:`doc_3d_rendering_limitations_color_banding` for "
"guidance on reducing banding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:809
#: ../../docs/tutorials/rendering/renderers.rst:258
msgid "Volumetric Fog"
msgstr "Brouillard volumétrique"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:811
msgid ""
"Volumetric fog provides a realistic fog effect to the scene, with fog color "
"being affected by the lights that traverse the fog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/environment_and_post_processing.rst:816
msgid ""
"See :ref:`doc_volumetric_fog` for documentation on setting up volumetric fog."
msgstr ""

